# Normalize line endings in the repository to LF.
#
# This team is mixed Windows/macOS. Without this, a Windows checkout commits
# CRLF and every file shows as wholly rewritten the moment someone on macOS
# touches it, which makes review useless and manufactures merge conflicts.
#
# Working copies still get native endings on checkout; only what git stores is
# normalized.
#
# Note for db/migrations: the migration runner already normalizes CRLF to LF
# before checksumming, so an already-applied file will not read as "drifted"
# just because a teammate is on a different OS. This rule keeps the stored
# bytes consistent as well.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated; collapse in diffs and never merge by hand.
package-lock.json linguist-generated=true -diff

# Binary, never touch.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf binary
